## HTTP Transport + x402 Tests

*These tests require the server running in HTTP mode. They test the transport layer, not business logic.*

| # | Test | Expected | Category |
|---|------|----------|----------|
| H1 | Health check endpoint | `GET /health` → 200, `{ status: "ok", version: "0.2.0", transport: "http" }` | Functionality |
| H2 | MCP tool call via HTTP | `POST /mcp` with verify-achievement → valid response | Functionality |
| H3 | x402 gated tool without payment | verify-achievement without payment header → 402 + payment instructions | Auth/Security |
| H4 | x402 gated tool with valid payment | verify-achievement with valid x402 header → 200 + tool response | Auth/Security |
| H5 | Free tool without payment | configure-policy without payment → 200 (no gating) | Auth/Security |
| H6 | Member identification via header | `X-Member-Id: maya-id` → resolves to learner role → child-scoped | Auth/Security |
| H7 | Missing member header defaults to manager | No X-Member-Id → default manager (backward compat) | Functionality |
| H8 | Concurrent sessions isolated | Parent + child connected simultaneously → independent state reads | Auth/Security |

---

## OWS Policy Tests (Bug #4 Fix)

| # | Test | Expected | Category |
|---|------|----------|----------|
| P1 | Manager ERC-20 to authorized wallet | Decode calldata `transfer(0xCHILD, amount)` → 0xCHILD in authorized_wallets → allow | Auth/Security |
| P2 | Manager ERC-20 to unauthorized wallet | Decode calldata `transfer(0xATTACKER, amount)` → not in authorized_wallets → deny | Auth/Security |
| P3 | Manager ERC-20 spend cap within limit | Decoded amount + daily_total < max_weekly → allow | Auth/Security |
| P4 | Manager ERC-20 spend cap exceeded | Decoded amount + daily_total > max_weekly → deny | Auth/Security |
| P5 | Non-ERC-20 transaction (native ETH) | `tx.data` empty or not transfer signature → deny (only ERC-20 USDC allowed) | Auth/Security |

