## Fitbit OAuth Flow Tests (D9)

| # | Test | Expected | Category |
|---|------|----------|----------|
| F1 | connect-fitbit returns valid OAuth URL | URL contains client_id, redirect_uri, scope=activity | Functionality |
| F2 | connect-fitbit is Manager only | Learner, Co-parent, Family, Advisor all denied | Auth/Security |
| F3 | Callback exchanges code for tokens (mock Fitbit API) | Access token + refresh token stored in fitbit-tokens.json | Functionality |
| F4 | Tokens stored encrypted | fitbit-tokens.json contents are AES-256-GCM encrypted, not plaintext | Auth/Security |
| F5 | Token auto-refresh on expiry | Expired access token → automatic refresh call → new token stored → API query succeeds | Functionality |
| F6 | verify-achievement with source "fitbit" queries API | Mock Fitbit returns 9,200 steps → score calculated from step count → achievement created with source: "fitbit" | Functionality |
| F7 | Missing FITBIT_CLIENT_ID env var | connect-fitbit returns graceful error: "Fitbit not configured" (not a crash) | Design/UX |
| F8 | verify-achievement source "fitbit" with no stored tokens | Returns error: "Fitbit not connected for this child. Use connect-fitbit first." | Design/UX |

